<div class="info-page privacy-notice-page" style="max-width: 860px; margin: var(--space-8) auto; padding: 0 var(--space-4);">
  <div class="alert alert-error" role="status" style="padding: var(--space-4); margin-bottom: var(--space-6);">
    <strong>Owner review draft — not approved for publication.</strong>
    Final publication remains gated on legal review of required controller/contact disclosures and legal bases, provider-region/transfer and retention evidence, and clean live-browser verification. No private residential address or fictitious business entity has been added.
  </div>
  <article class="card" style="padding: var(--space-6); border: var(--border-thick); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--color-surface-card);">
    <h1 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--font-size-2xl); margin-bottom: var(--space-2);">Privacy Notice</h1>
    <p style="font-size: var(--font-size-sm); color: var(--color-ink-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-6);">Private beta review draft · Source review: 19 October 2026</p>
    <h2>Who runs The Vinyl Drop (responsible operator)</h2>
    <p>The Vinyl Drop is a free, invite-only vinyl community website run by Jaap Hopman as a private individual, not by a company. The public privacy contact is <a href="mailto:<%= contactEmail %>"><%= contactEmail %></a>. Required controller/contact disclosures are being checked for this specific arrangement; this draft does not publish a residential address or invent a legal entity.</p>
    <h2>What the application handles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Account and sign-in:</strong> email address, Supabase Auth identity, authentication/session state and security information. Supabase Auth and relevant providers handle password sign-in and Google OAuth; application tables do not store plaintext passwords.</li>
      <li><strong>Profile:</strong> username, display name, avatar URL, optional website, bio, coarse location and timestamps. Public profile fields rendered by the site may be visible. Location is intended to be city/neighbourhood level, not a street address.</li>
      <li><strong>Records and listings:</strong> release/catalogue details, format, physical-copy condition, price or trade indication, description, publication state and timestamps.</li>
      <li><strong>Photos:</strong> processed listing images, Storage paths, order and alt text. Supported uploads are converted to WebP, resized and stripped of EXIF metadata. Published listing photos use a public-read path; do not upload private or sensitive images.</li>
      <li><strong>Community activity:</strong> comments, favorites and activity events. Comments on visible listings are public. Favorites are private. Some activity event types appear on community activity surfaces.</li>
      <li><strong>Registration audit:</strong> accepted Terms version, Terms acceptance timestamp, minimum-age attestation timestamp and linked Auth user ID are stored in a restricted private database table. No date of birth or identity document is collected solely for the age check.</li>
      <li><strong>Security and operations:</strong> application/platform logs, limited error diagnostics, authentication cookies and password-safety check requests. Provider-side log retention has not yet been verified.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How information is used</h2>
    <p>The application uses information to authenticate users, maintain profiles, manage listings and photos, show public content, support discovery, enable community features, protect accounts and the service, and investigate operational/security faults. For the password-safety check, only a five-character SHA-1 hash prefix is sent to the Have I Been Pwned range API; the matching suffix is compared locally.</p>
    <p><strong>Legal-basis review remains open.</strong> Contract necessity is a candidate basis for data needed to provide user-requested core functions. Legitimate interests are a candidate basis for necessary security/abuse prevention, subject to a documented balancing assessment. These are candidates, not a claim that a legal adviser has validated each basis.</p>
    <h2>What is visible to other users</h2>
    <p>Published listings and their photos, public comments, and the public profile fields rendered by the site can be seen by visitors. Favorites are not public. Activity visibility depends on event type. Do not put personal details you do not want to share in a public profile, listing or comment.</p>
    <h2>Services and external requests</h2>
    <p>Different features use different providers; not every provider receives every category of data. The application uses Supabase for Auth, PostgreSQL and Storage, and Render for hosting/runtime. Resend is used only by configured mail routes; Strato only for the domain/DNS/mail functions actually configured. Discogs and/or MusicBrainz may receive catalogue search terms when lookups are requested. Have I Been Pwned receives the password hash prefix described above. Google participates in OAuth sign-in through the configured authentication flow.</p>
    <p>Actual provider regions, international transfers and safeguards, provider-side logs/backups, and processing terms still need independent verification. This notice does not claim EU-only processing or a fixed provider retention period.</p>
    <h2>Cookies and fonts</h2>
    <p>The source configures essential HTTP-only authentication/session cookies for access, refresh, recovery and short-lived PKCE/auth-flow handling. It also uses <code>tvd-beta-welcome-seen</code> as a first-party, HTTP-only presentation marker for 180 days and <code>tvd-beta-welcome</code> as a 60-second, HTTP-only display-only flash. Neither cookie grants account or beta access.</p>
    <p>Font families are served from this site's own <code>/fonts/</code> assets under the SIL Open Font License; external Google Fonts links have been removed from the layout source. A clean deployed-browser/network check is still required before a definitive statement that no other third-party requests or tracking storage occur.</p>
    <h2>Waitlist</h2>
    <p>The application is not collecting waitlist addresses. This pilot has no public waitlist, email-capture form or commercial newsletter.</p>
    <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Active account/profile:</strong> kept while the account is active; there is no automatic one-year expiry for an active account.</li>
      <li><strong>Archived listing data/photos:</strong> target deletion 12 months after archiving, except for a specific documented reason to retain particular data longer. This is a policy target, not an implemented automatic-deletion promise.</li>
      <li><strong>Comments, favorites and activity:</strong> kept only while needed for service/community purposes. On a valid account-erasure request, remove or anonymise linked records where appropriate while considering other users' rights and specific legal/security needs.</li>
      <li><strong>Registration agreement audit:</strong> the minimum Terms-version and timestamp record is linked to the Auth account and is deleted when that Auth identity is erased.</li>
      <li><strong>Routine application/security logs:</strong> approximately 30 days is the target policy period. Incident-specific material may be retained longer only when necessary and documented; actual provider retention is not verified.</li>
      <li><strong>Privacy-request audit:</strong> a minimal, access-controlled record is targeted for deletion within 12 months after closure unless a specific documented need requires longer.</li>
      <li><strong>Backups and provider logs:</strong> actual retention limits are provider-controlled and remain to be checked. After a restore, valid deletions must be re-applied where necessary.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Archived does not mean deleted. The app does not currently offer a self-service full account export or erasure flow. A valid request may require manual work across Auth, database rows, Storage objects, diagnostics, provider logs and backups. No automatic expiry/deletion should be inferred from these policy targets.</p>
    <h2>Minimum age and beta access</h2>
    <p>The initial pilot is for adults aged 18 or older and is invite-only. Registration uses a self-attestation only; no birth date or ID is requested solely to verify age. The Google OAuth Console test-user list and the application's private-beta email allowlist are separate access controls. There is no public waitlist or marketing newsletter.</p>
    <h2>Your privacy rights and requests</h2>
    <p>Depending on the applicable legal basis and circumstances, you may request access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability, or object to certain processing. Where consent is the legal basis for a purpose, you may withdraw it. These rights have statutory conditions and exceptions. Contact <a href="mailto:<%= contactEmail %>"><%= contactEmail %></a>; identity checks should be proportionate and responses are normally due within one month under GDPR, subject to lawful extensions.</p>
    <p>You can complain to the Dutch supervisory authority, the <a href="https://autoriteitpersoonsgegevens.nl/nl/onderwerpen/algemene-informatie-avg/rechten-van-betrokkenen" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens (AP)</a>.</p>
    <h2>Manual requests and security incidents</h2>
    <p>The project follows a manual privacy-request procedure while self-service export/erasure is unavailable. The internal runbook covers containment, scope assessment, safe evidence preservation, risk assessment and required notification for personal-data breaches. The notice and runbook remain review drafts until the specified owner/privacy checks have been completed.</p>
